01:07:11,717 --> 01:07:12,617
- No thank you,

1464
01:07:12,717 --> 01:07:13,983
I've got to get back
to the city,

1465
01:07:14,083 --> 01:07:15,717
Will you drive me
to the station, Dr, Foster?

1466
01:07:15,817 --> 01:07:16,783
- I'll be glad to,

1467
01:07:16,883 --> 01:07:18,083
- But what about the interview?

1468
01:07:18,183 --> 01:07:19,917
- Well, that'll have to wait
until some other time,

1469
01:07:20,017 --> 01:07:21,917
I just remembered
an appointment at the office,

1470
01:07:22,017 --> 01:07:25,150
so I've got to catch
the next train,

1471
01:07:25,250 --> 01:07:26,450
If you'll excuse me, Countess?

1472
01:07:26,550 --> 01:07:28,383
- Yes, I will excuse you,

1473
01:07:28,483 --> 01:07:29,717
JOEL:
And then I'll slap you,

1474
01:07:29,817 --> 01:07:32,817
- Professor, do you also make
a hobby of collecting coffins?

1475
01:07:32,917 --> 01:07:34,950
- Why yes,
in a manner of speaking,

1476
01:07:35,050 --> 01:07:38,150
I find a coffin much more
comfortable than a bed,

1477
01:07:38,250 --> 01:07:39,150
CROW [IMITATES LUGOSI]:
It's a water coffin,

1478
01:07:39,250 --> 01:07:41,183
- Many people do so, my dear,

1479
01:07:41,283 --> 01:07:43,883
Is it so strange
that I accept one

1480
01:07:43,983 --> 01:07:46,217
while waiting
for eternal rest?

1481
01:07:46,317 --> 01:07:48,183
- No, I suppose not,

1482
01:07:48,283 --> 01:07:50,183
Well, thank you
for your hospitality,

1483
01:07:50,283 --> 01:07:52,050
Goodbye,

1484
01:07:52,150 --> 01:07:53,783
TOM:
Wait, it is strange,

1485
01:07:53,883 --> 01:07:56,117
- I trust
we will meet again,

1486
01:07:56,217 --> 01:07:58,850
It has been so nice
meeting you,

1487
01:07:58,950 --> 01:08:00,383
JOEL:
What a sweet couple,

1488
01:08:01,550 --> 01:08:02,550
CROW:
Kooky,

1489
01:08:05,350 --> 01:08:07,183
- Don't tell me
I'm still dreaming,

1490
01:08:07,283 --> 01:08:08,183
- Well, what do you mean?

1491
01:08:08,283 --> 01:08:10,817
- That gravedigger,
he's real, isn't he?

1492
01:08:10,917 --> 01:08:12,383
JOEL:
What gravedigger?

1493
01:08:14,550 --> 01:08:15,750
- Oh, he's real alright,

1494
01:08:15,850 --> 01:08:17,483
But I hardly think
he's a gravedigger,

1495
01:08:17,583 --> 01:08:19,550
More likely laying
the foundation for a house,

1496
01:08:19,650 --> 01:08:21,783
- You're a trusting soul,
aren't you, Doctor?

1497
01:08:21,883 --> 01:08:22,783
- Is that a crime?

1498
01:08:22,883 --> 01:08:25,383
- No, on the contrary,
I envy you,

1499
01:08:25,483 --> 01:08:26,383
- Are you trying
to make me believe

1500
01:08:26,483 --> 01:08:27,883
you're one of those
hard boiled reporters

1501
01:08:27,983 --> 01:08:29,583
that we read about
or see in the movies?

1502
01:08:29,683 --> 01:08:31,017
- No, but working
on a newspaper,

1503
01:08:31,117 --> 01:08:33,717
one becomes cynical
and suspicious,

1504
01:08:33,817 --> 01:08:36,117
CROW:
Aw, she writes for Crappy Dick,

1505
01:08:51,583 --> 01:08:52,483
What a bucket of bolts,

1506
01:08:52,583 --> 01:08:53,850
- I've enjoyed meeting you,
Miss Hunter,

1507
01:08:53,950 --> 01:08:55,383
I hope to have the pleasure
of seeing you again,

1508
01:08:55,483 --> 01:08:57,150
- I have a hunch you will,
Doctor Foster,

1509
01:08:57,250 --> 01:08:58,150
TOM:
You have a hunch too?

1510
01:08:58,250 --> 01:08:59,917
I guess it's contagious,

1511
01:09:00,017 --> 01:09:01,817
- ,,,just why did you
come up here,

1512
01:09:01,917 --> 01:09:03,050
or is it a secret?

1513
01:09:03,150 --> 01:09:07,383
- It is, but somehow I feel
that I can trust you,

1514
01:09:07,483 --> 01:09:08,517
- You can,

1515
01:09:08,617 --> 01:09:10,817
- You've heard of the case
of the vanishing brides?

1516
01:09:10,917 --> 01:09:12,150
- Why, surely,

1517
01:09:12,250 --> 01:09:14,283
- I think I have a clue,

1518
01:09:14,383 --> 01:09:15,483
- You don't mean
that you suspect,,,

1519
01:09:15,583 --> 01:09:17,550
- Yes, I do,

1520
01:09:17,650 --> 01:09:19,550
I wanna show you something,

1521
01:09:20,917 --> 01:09:21,917
What are these?

1522
01:09:22,017 --> 01:09:23,417
- Why, they're orchids,
of course,

1523
01:09:23,517 --> 01:09:24,917
- You bet they're orchids,

1524
01:09:25,017 --> 01:09:27,117
And they didn't grow
in my dreams,

1525
01:09:27,217 --> 01:09:29,750
They're exactly likely the one
that disappeared from my bag,

1526
01:09:29,850 --> 01:09:31,283
TOM:
They grew in,,, [indistinct],

1527
01:09:31,383 --> 01:09:33,817
- I found them on the floor
beside my bed this morning,

1528
01:09:33,917 --> 01:09:35,483
The person who came
into my room last night

1529
01:09:35,583 --> 01:09:37,117
must've brought these with him,

1530
01:09:37,217 --> 01:09:39,117
That seems like
a logical explanation,

1531
01:09:39,217 --> 01:09:40,750
- There's
no question about it,

1532
01:09:40,850 --> 01:09:42,883
Honestly, Doctor,
don't you remember

1533
01:09:42,983 --> 01:09:45,050
meeting me in the hallway
last night,

1534
01:09:45,150 --> 01:09:46,550
- No, I don't,

1535
01:09:46,650 --> 01:09:49,883
And if I did I--
I must've been asleep,

1536
01:09:49,983 --> 01:09:52,650
- Either that,
or you were hypnotized,

1537
01:09:52,750 --> 01:09:54,817
- Yes, that's quite possible,

1538
01:09:54,917 --> 01:09:57,083
CROW:
He may still be,

1539
01:09:57,183 --> 01:09:58,717
TOM:
[indistinct],

1540
01:09:58,817 --> 01:09:59,717
JOEL:
Looks like a train,

1541
01:09:59,817 --> 01:10:01,983
but he'll need proof,

1542
01:10:02,083 --> 01:10:03,717
- Well, watch your step,

1543
01:10:03,817 --> 01:10:05,650
And if you discover
anything, call me,

1544
01:10:05,750 --> 01:10:07,150
- That's a promise,
- Goodbye,

1545
01:10:07,250 --> 01:10:08,750
- Not goodbye, au revoir,

1546
01:10:08,850 --> 01:10:10,417
CROW:
No, not au revoir, ciao,

1547
01:10:10,517 --> 01:10:11,717
No, not ciao, aloha,

1548
01:10:11,817 --> 01:10:13,517
No, not aloha, aufiderzein!

1549
01:10:13,617 --> 01:10:15,383
- Alright,
print the story on page one,

1550
01:10:15,483 --> 01:10:16,783
[JOEL MUFFLED SPEECH]

1551
01:10:16,883 --> 01:10:17,983
- ,,,fingers crossed
that this paper

1552
01:10:18,083 --> 01:10:19,583
isn't sued for libel
by some of these phony suspects

1553
01:10:19,683 --> 01:10:20,683
that the police
are bringing in,

1554
01:10:20,783 --> 01:10:22,017
[JOEL MUFFLED SPEECH]

1555
01:10:22,117 --> 01:10:23,550
,,,get me a [INDISTINCT] outta
the guy they just brought in,

1556
01:10:23,650 --> 01:10:26,417
- I don't want photographs,
I want real clues,

1557
01:10:26,517 --> 01:10:28,317
If the DA's office
can't pick up the madman

1558
01:10:28,417 --> 01:10:29,883
who's stealing the bodies
of these dead girls,

1559
01:10:29,983 --> 01:10:31,083
maybe we can,

1560
01:10:31,183 --> 01:10:33,150
- Okay, I'll throw it
in the wastebasket,

1561
01:10:33,250 --> 01:10:35,350
JOEL: The script?
- No, have it developed,

1562
01:10:35,450 --> 01:10:36,883
[indistinct]
Where's Lefty?

1563
01:10:36,983 --> 01:10:38,217
- Over at Central Station,

1564
01:10:38,317 --> 01:10:39,217
- The only thing
he gets over there

1565
01:10:39,317 --> 01:10:40,250
is a game of gin rummy,

1566
01:10:40,350 --> 01:10:41,383
Tell him to get back here,

1567
01:10:41,483 --> 01:10:42,383
- Well, I got something,

1568
01:10:42,483 --> 01:10:44,217
- I'll say you have,
you're fired,

1569
01:10:44,317 --> 01:10:45,883
- What do you mean?
You can't do that to me,

1570
01:10:45,983 --> 01:10:47,017
- Listen, just because

1571
01:10:47,117 --> 01:10:48,383
the bodies of dead girls
disappear

1572
01:10:48,483 --> 01:10:50,417
is no reason
you can do a vanishing act,

1573
01:10:50,517 --> 01:10:51,683
- But you gave me
the assignment,

1574
01:10:51,783 --> 01:10:52,683
Yeah, I suppose I did,

1575
01:10:52,783 --> 01:10:53,850
Alright,
where have you been?

1576
01:10:53,950 --> 01:10:55,050
What've you uncovered?

1577
01:10:55,150 --> 01:10:56,483
- Well, hey, not so fast,

1578
01:10:56,583 --> 01:10:58,450
Listen, Mr, Keenan,
last night I went through

1579
01:10:58,550 --> 01:11:00,283
the most gruesome
experience of my life,

1580
01:11:00,383 --> 01:11:01,283
- You should talk,

1581
01:11:01,383 --> 01:11:02,950
All of my life
has been a nightmare,

1582
01:11:03,050 --> 01:11:05,883
- Well, you can rest easier now,
because I've seen plenty,

1583
01:11:05,983 --> 01:11:07,583
If I can only prove
I wasn't dreaming,

1584
01:11:07,683 --> 01:11:09,017
- Dreaming?

1585
01:11:09,117 --> 01:11:10,917
- I had a dream
last night myself,

1586
01:11:11,017 --> 01:11:13,350
I dreamed you gave me that raise
you been promising me,

1587
01:11:13,450 --> 01:11:15,050
TOM:
Thank you, Shecky,

1588
01:11:15,150 --> 01:11:16,983
- ,,,go on with
your dream story,

1589
01:11:17,083 --> 01:11:18,717
- Well, there's a certain
Professor Lorenz

1590
01:11:18,817 --> 01:11:20,050
that lives upstate,

1591
01:11:20,150 --> 01:11:21,150
He knows all about orchids

1592
01:11:21,250 --> 01:11:23,317
but insists that he doesn't
grow them anymore,

1593
01:11:23,417 --> 01:11:25,883
Yet, I found these
in my bedroom this morning,

1594
01:11:27,250 --> 01:11:28,783
- Listen [indistinct]
you didn't go off someplace

1595
01:11:28,883 --> 01:11:29,783
and get married, did you?

1596
01:11:29,883 --> 01:11:30,950
- No, I didn't,

1597
01:11:31,050 --> 01:11:34,150
But I saw the bodies
of those other missing brides,

1598
01:11:34,250 --> 01:11:36,283
- Alright,
Now take it easy,

1599
01:11:36,383 --> 01:11:39,550
Stop breathing hard, Pat,
and tell me all about it,

1600
01:11:39,650 --> 01:11:41,683
Did you really see
any bodies?

1601
01:11:41,783 --> 01:11:43,550
- Yes, and no,

1602
01:11:43,650 --> 01:11:45,783
- I see,
Just a bit of ectoplasm,

1603
01:11:45,883 --> 01:11:47,383
JOEL:
Yeah, on the front
of your jacket,

1604
01:11:47,483 --> 01:11:49,917
- ,,,only,,,
Oh, I can't explain it,

1605
01:11:50,017 --> 01:11:52,017
- Yeah, you know something
the same way I am,

1606
01:11:52,117 --> 01:11:53,650
I see brides everywhere,

1607
01:11:53,750 --> 01:11:55,983
hear wedding bells
ringing in my ears,

1608
01:11:56,083 --> 01:11:57,550
- And I saw a dead man too,

1609
01:11:57,650 --> 01:11:59,850
ALL:
And his hair was perfect!

1610
01:11:59,950 --> 01:12:02,317
- Very well,

1611
01:12:02,417 --> 01:12:03,450
JOEL:
Hubba, hubba, what a suit,

1612
01:12:03,550 --> 01:12:05,150
Let me clean that off,
- ,,,I'm sorry,

1613
01:12:05,250 --> 01:12:06,950
She's busy,
she's with Mr, Keenan,

1614
01:12:07,050 --> 01:12:08,117
- It's very important
that I see her,

1615
01:12:08,217 --> 01:12:09,117
I'm Dr, Foster,

1616
01:12:09,217 --> 01:12:10,950
I wonder if you'd mind
announcing me,

1617
01:12:11,050 --> 01:12:12,850
TOM:
And now, right here
in our very office,

1618
01:12:12,950 --> 01:12:16,150
a very talented young Doctor,
please welcome,,,

1619
01:12:16,250 --> 01:12:17,683
- ,,,insists on seeing
Miss Hunter,

1620
01:12:17,783 --> 01:12:19,817
- Tell him he can have
all of her time from now on,

1621
01:12:19,917 --> 01:12:21,917
- That's the Dr, Foster
I was telling you about,

1622
01:12:22,017 --> 01:12:23,550
Maybe he has more evidence,

1623
01:12:24,617 --> 01:12:26,850
- Alright,
send the saw bones in,

1624
01:12:26,950 --> 01:12:28,183
- Hey look,
if you don't mind,

1625
01:12:28,283 --> 01:12:30,817
I'm going out
for a nervous breakdown,

1626
01:12:30,917 --> 01:12:32,417
TOM:
Funny!

1627
01:12:32,517 --> 01:12:34,483
- Well Doctor,
you almost beat me here,

1628
01:12:34,583 --> 01:12:35,583
- Yes, I drove down,

1629
01:12:35,683 --> 01:12:37,517
- Dr, Foster,
Mr, Keenan, my editor,

1630
01:12:37,617 --> 01:12:38,617
- Very nice to meet you,
Mr, Keenan,

1631
01:12:38,717 --> 01:12:40,350
- How do you do?
This cub reporter of mine

1632
01:12:40,450 --> 01:12:41,717
has been telling me
a weird story

1633
01:12:41,817 --> 01:12:44,217
about a certain Dr, Lorenz
up in your neighborhood,

1634
01:12:44,317 --> 01:12:47,083
- It's weird alright,
but I'm confident it's true,

1635
01:12:47,183 --> 01:12:48,750
After you left,
I looked around the station

1636
01:12:48,850 --> 01:12:50,350
to find out if Lorenz
had any other coffins

1637
01:12:50,450 --> 01:12:51,550
assigned to him,

1638
01:12:51,650 --> 01:12:54,350
I found the consignment alright,
but instead of a coffin,

1639
01:12:54,450 --> 01:12:56,150
it was a box
filled with this stuff,

1640
01:12:56,250 --> 01:12:58,217
CROW:
Olive loaf,

1641
01:12:58,317 --> 01:13:00,417
- So what?
That's ordinary garden moss,

1642
01:13:00,517 --> 01:13:02,817
- It's moss, alright,
But not ordinary,

1643
01:13:02,917 --> 01:13:04,450
This is a special type
used by florists

1644
01:13:04,550 --> 01:13:06,683
and hybridizers
for growing orchids,

1645
01:13:06,783 --> 01:13:07,850
It's called ozmondin,

1646
01:13:07,950 --> 01:13:09,017
ALL [MUMBLING]:
Ozmondin?

1647
01:13:09,117 --> 01:13:10,483
- ,,,he does grow orchids
like these,

1648
01:13:10,583 --> 01:13:11,650
And the same kind were worn

1649
01:13:11,750 --> 01:13:13,750
by every one of the brides
that died,

1650
01:13:13,850 --> 01:13:15,383
- Well, maybe it is a clue,

1651
01:13:15,483 --> 01:13:17,583
But how do I know that the rest
isn't a cockeyed nightmare?

1652
01:13:17,683 --> 01:13:18,817
CROW:
Or a night-eyed cock-mare,

1653
01:13:18,917 --> 01:13:20,417
- ,,,you don't remember
talking to her,

1654
01:13:20,517 --> 01:13:21,417
- I could've talked to her

1655
01:13:21,517 --> 01:13:22,983
while in a somnambulistic
state,

1656
01:13:23,083 --> 01:13:24,650
under the influence
of hypnotism,

1657
01:13:24,750 --> 01:13:26,217
- Aw, now wait a minute,

1658
01:13:26,317 --> 01:13:28,250
Are you trying to tell me
that this Professor Lorenz

1659
01:13:28,350 --> 01:13:30,583
is a hypnotist
as well as a horticulturist?

1660
01:13:30,683 --> 01:13:32,083
JOEL:
And a ventriloquist,

1661
01:13:32,183 --> 01:13:33,583
- My short acquaintance with him
has convinced me

1662
01:13:33,683 --> 01:13:35,617
that he's a man
of unlimited talents,

1663
01:13:35,717 --> 01:13:37,550
He's strange, peculiar,

1664
01:13:37,650 --> 01:13:40,383
I've even suspected him
of being insane,

1665
01:13:40,483 --> 01:13:42,183
But the fact remains,
he's not only a doctor,

1666
01:13:42,283 --> 01:13:44,283
but a physicist and a scientist
of great ability,

1667
01:13:44,383 --> 01:13:45,417
TOM:
And a horticulturist,

1668
01:13:45,517 --> 01:13:46,683
- ,,,this hotheaded wife of his?

1669
01:13:46,783 --> 01:13:49,150
- I hesitate to bring her
into the case at all,

1670
01:13:49,250 --> 01:13:50,550
Professional ethics
forbid a doctor

1671
01:13:50,650 --> 01:13:52,350
talking
about his patients,

1672
01:13:52,450 --> 01:13:54,450
- Oh, forget about
your ethics, Doctor,

1673
01:13:54,550 --> 01:13:56,650
After all,
we're after a criminal,

1674
01:13:56,750 --> 01:13:58,750
How does this woman
fit into the picture?

1675
01:13:58,850 --> 01:13:59,917
Come on,,,

1676
01:14:00,017 --> 01:14:00,983
JOEL:
Just clearing him up
a little bit there,

1677
01:14:01,083 --> 01:14:02,183
- ,,,curious fact about her is

1678
01:14:02,283 --> 01:14:04,717
that although she has
the appearance of a young woman,

1679
01:14:04,817 --> 01:14:05,883
her heart and arteries
indicate

1680
01:14:05,983 --> 01:14:08,450
that she's at least
70 or 80 years old,

1681
01:14:08,550 --> 01:14:10,283
- Well, that doesn't
explain anything,

1682
01:14:10,383 --> 01:14:11,383
It certainly
doesn't explain why,,,

1683
01:14:11,483 --> 01:14:12,383
TOM:
It's tidy, now,

1684
01:14:12,483 --> 01:14:13,383
- ,,,should steal
these dead girls,

1685
01:14:13,483 --> 01:14:14,383
JOEL:
Nice and clean,

1686
01:14:14,483 --> 01:14:16,017
- It's possible
they may still be alive,

1687
01:14:16,117 --> 01:14:17,717
- Alive in a cataleptic state?

1688
01:14:17,817 --> 01:14:18,917
TOM:
Iowa?

1689
01:14:19,017 --> 01:14:21,217
- Alright, alright,
What are your other deductions?

1690
01:14:21,317 --> 01:14:22,617
- Simply this,

1691
01:14:22,717 --> 01:14:24,450
These young girls,
whether dead or alive,

1692
01:14:24,550 --> 01:14:26,750
are being used by Lorenz
in some manner,

1693
01:14:26,850 --> 01:14:27,750
as human guinea pigs

1694
01:14:27,850 --> 01:14:29,617
to sustain his wife
in a youthful state,

1695
01:14:29,717 --> 01:14:31,317
TOM: Bride juice,
- Oh, that's preposterous,

1696
01:14:31,417 --> 01:14:32,750
- It's nothing of the kind,

1697
01:14:32,850 --> 01:14:34,217
Scientists are finding out
every day

1698
01:14:34,317 --> 01:14:35,883
that glands and hormones
have a lot to do

1699
01:14:35,983 --> 01:14:37,317
with life and health,
JOEL: Yeah!

1700
01:14:37,417 --> 01:14:38,617
- The glands in our bodies
help determine

1701
01:14:38,717 --> 01:14:40,983
the condition of our teeth,
the texture of our hair,,,

1702
01:14:41,083 --> 01:14:43,083
